Sure! Below is a simple example of a rotating card using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it will rotate 180 degrees around its Y‑axis.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
  /* Container that holds the card */
  .card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
  }

  /* The card itself */
  .card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D transforms */
    position: relative;
  }

  /* Front side of the card */
  .card .front,
  .card .back {
    backface-visibility: hidden;      /* Hide the backside when rotated */
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 12px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
  }

  .card .front {
    background: #f9f9f9;
  }

  .card .back {
    background: #e0e0e0;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);       /* Place back side behind front */
  }

  /* Hover effect – rotate the card */
  .card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">Front Side</div>
    <div class="back">Back Side</div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` has `perspective: 1000px;` to give a 3D depth effect.
2. **Transform style** – The card uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its children keep their 3D positions.
3. **Backface visibility** – Both sides have `backface-visibility: hidden;` so the hidden side doesn’t show through.
4. **Hover** – On hover, the card rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side.

Feel free to replace the text or add images inside `.front` and `.back` to suit your design. Enjoy!
